-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/c7e8aef4-42a0-5ae0-b126-0f269595ff7a
-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner leg laws: Wα=β⟨ d⟩τ, Wβ=α⟨ d'⟩τ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \nmid M$ and $M \ge 5$, and a ring embedding $\iota \colon \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ into $\mathbb C$. The hypothesis `hβdef` is [`ModularCurve.HeckeBetaOneDefined (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator.html#L84), i.e. for every $y$ in [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) (the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions of ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$) the Laurent series $y(q^p)$, obtained by multiplying all exponents by $p$ via [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), lies in [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142), the corresponding field for $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp^2)$.
--
--   Two pairs of matrix data are fixed. First, integers $y, w_0$ with $p w_0 - M y = 1$ and elements $\gamma, \gamma' \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with
--   $$\gamma = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & y \\ M & p w_0\end{pmatrix}, \qquad \gamma' = \begin{pmatrix} w_0 & -y \\ -M & p\end{pmatrix}.$$
--   Second, integers $y_2, w_2$ with $p^2 w_2 - M y_2 = 1$ and $\delta, \delta' \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with
--   $$\delta = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & y_2 \\ M & p^2 w_2\end{pmatrix}, \qquad \delta' = \begin{pmatrix} w_2 & -y_2 \\ -M & p^2\end{pmatrix}.$$
--   Throughout, [`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix n`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21) denotes the element of $GL_2(\mathbb R)$ that is upper triangular with diagonal entries $n, 1$ (and is the identity for $n = 0$), so that its action on the upper half-plane is $z \mapsto n z$, and $\mid[k]$ is the weight-$k$ slash action.
--
--   The first automorphism is $\tau$, an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137). The hypothesis `hτ` has four conjuncts, all phrased through the coefficientwise map $\iota_* =$ [`ModularCurve.coeffMap ι`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) from $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ to $\mathbb C((q))$ and the $q$-expansions `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion 1` of weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ (viewed as a subgroup of $GL_2(\mathbb R)$), read as Hahn series over $\mathbb Z$:
--
--   (i) *Presentations.* For every $x$ in the field there are an integer $k$ and forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ such that the $q$-expansion of $g$ is nonzero, $\iota_*(x)$ equals the quotient of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, and moreover: there are a form $\varphi$ and a nonzero integer $D$ with $\varphi = D \cdot \bigl((f \mid[k] \gamma)(\mathrm{diag}(p,1) \cdot z)\bigr)$ as functions on the upper half-plane; likewise $\psi$ and $E \neq 0$ with $\psi = E \cdot ((g \mid[k] \gamma)(\mathrm{diag}(p,1)\cdot z))$; and likewise $\varphi', D' \neq 0$ and $\psi', E' \neq 0$ for $f$ and $g$ slashed by $\gamma'$ instead of $\gamma$.
--
--   (ii) *Transport by $\tau$.* For all $x$, all $k$, all forms $f, g, \varphi, \psi$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ and all nonzero integers $D, E$ such that $\varphi = D\cdot((f\mid[k]\gamma)(\mathrm{diag}(p,1)\cdot z))$, $\psi = E\cdot((g\mid[k]\gamma)(\mathrm{diag}(p,1)\cdot z))$, the $q$-expansion of $g$ is nonzero and $\iota_*(x)$ is the quotient of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x) = (E/D)\cdot$ (the $q$-expansion of $\varphi$ divided by that of $\psi$), the scalar entering as the constant Hahn series `HahnSeries.C ((E : ℂ) / (D : ℂ))`.
--
--   (iii) *Transport by $\tau^{-1}$.* The same implication with $\gamma'$ in place of $\gamma$ and $\tau^{-1}$ in place of $\tau$.
--
--   (iv) *Normalisation on $j$.* For every $j$ in the field whose underlying Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (that is, $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`), the underlying Laurent series of $\tau j$ is the image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), i.e. of $j(q^p)$.
--
--   The second automorphism is $W$, an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103). The hypothesis `hW` consists of the four conjuncts of exactly the same shape as (i)–(iv), with: forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp^2)$ in place of forms on $\Gamma_1(Mp)$; the matrices $\delta, \delta'$ in place of $\gamma, \gamma'$; [`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix (p ^ 2)`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21), acting as $z \mapsto p^2 z$, in place of $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$; $W$ and $W^{-1}$ in place of $\tau$ and $\tau^{-1}$; and, in the normalisation clause, the image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ (p ^ 2) ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), i.e. $j(q^{p^2})$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist natural numbers $d$ and $d'$, each coprime to $Mp$, such that the following two identities of maps hold, where $\alpha =$ [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaOneBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator.html#L66) is the inclusion of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (x1FunctionField (M * p))` into `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * p))`, $\beta =$ [`ModularCurve.heckeBetaOneBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator.html#L116) is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra map between the same two fields induced by $q \mapsto q^p$ (this being the branch selected because `hβdef` holds), and [`ModularCurve.diamondAutBar (M * p) d`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L94) is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, in the sense of [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24), of the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137):
--
--   first, for every $x$ in [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182),
--   $$W(\alpha(x)) = \beta\bigl(\langle d\rangle(\tau x)\bigr);$$
--   second, for every such $x$,
--   $$W(\beta(x)) = \alpha\bigl(\langle d'\rangle(\tau x)\bigr).$$
--   Only the existence of such $d, d'$ coprime to $Mp$ is asserted; no congruence determining them is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the Atkin–Lehner involution at $p$ with the two degeneracy maps $\alpha$ (inclusion) and $\beta$ ($q \mapsto q^p$) from the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ into that of $X(\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp^2))$, in the form of a pair of "leg laws" in which the two legs are interchanged up to a diamond operator and the fixed automorphism $\tau$. It is used in the assembly of the full Atkin–Lehner statement, namely by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_coprime_algEquiv_algEquiv_apply_heckeAlphaOneBar_eq_heckeBetaOneBar_diamondAutBar_and_apply_heckeBetaOneBar_eq_of_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_coprime_algEquiv_algEquiv_apply_heckeAlphaOneBar_eq_heckeBetaOneBar_diamondAutBar_and_apply_heckeBetaOneBar_eq_of_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_coprime_apply_heckeAlphaOneBar_eq_heckeBetaOneBar_diamondAutBar_of_atkinLehnerSlash_p_of_atkinLehnerSlash_sq.lean

